  "proved_reduction": [
    "Any reduced pair for a nontrivial decomposition of a least-weight essential disk has a positive-Euler disk summand after the already drafted sphere/RP2 exclusions. Its boundary must be inessential, since an essential summand has strictly lower normal weight.",
    "The other connected summand has chi=0 and boundary, hence is an annulus or Mobius band. Coherent pairings make all possible circles intrinsically two-sided in both surfaces; all such circles separate both, contrary to reducedness. Only proper arcs remain, each nonseparating in H.",
    "Cutting k arcs gives k+1 disk patches in P and k in H. The P adjacency tree has at least two leaf disk patches, both positive weight.",
    "Boundary compression of H along a minimum-weight leaf E gives an embedded PL disk of weight w(H)+2w(E)<=w(F). If its boundary is essential, least normal weight forces equality throughout."
  ],
  "not_proved": [
    "The boundary-compressed disk has essential boundary.",
    "The original full fundamental or primitive vertex-disk theorem."
  ],
  "research_caution": "An inessential-boundary disk in a reducible manifold need not be boundary parallel. Its capped sphere cannot silently be declared to bound a ball."
